==Battleground==
*1 [[Brollow]] spawns after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**30 [[Brollow]]s spawn, delay 0.67~2 seconds<sup>20f~60f</sup>.
**5 [[Brollow]]s spawn, delay 1.33~2.67 seconds<sup>40f~80f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Brollow]]s spawn, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Miz Devil]]s spawn, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.
**15 [[Miz Devil]]s spawn, delay 2~4 seconds<sup>60f~120f</sup>.
**1 [[Flying Ninja Cat (Enemy)|Flying Ninja Cat]] spawns.

==Strategy==
This stage is similar to [[Heavenly Tower/Floor 22|the original Floor 22]], having an onslaught of stronger Brollows compared to the original version along with Flying Ninja Cat, now supported by an additional horde of Miz Devils. Stall the Brollow at the beginning, use slower units as to not hit the base before fully prepared, and face the many enemies in a row. [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]], like in the original version, is great for dealing with everything here, as a couple of hits will take down the Miz Devils, usually 2 hits for the Brollows, and they're great at dealing with the Flying Ninja. [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapstick Cats]] are also effective at doing the same, and they stand further giving them even more safety from the threats. [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Slime Cat/Jelly Dumpling]] is an absolute beast here, being able to oneshot the Brollows and take out 55% of Miz Devil's shield with its very expansive Wave at level 40, in additon to being relatively disposable. [[:Category:Shield Piercing Cats|Shield Piercing Cats]] aren't too recommended here, as the Miz Devils only have a shield of 60,000 HP that never regenerates, though [[Ancient Egg: N109 (Rare Cat)|Barrel Cat]] may be an exception thanks to its Area Attacks and fairly long range plus Long Distance, which can also hit Miz Devils behind Flying Ninja Cat. Simply bring more Ranged Attackers and Area Attackers to deal with them.

You can easily stall for money with [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone Cat]] and a Research Combo, as it can knockback the Brollow and take a hit before disappearing. Once it dies, just wait for the money.

